#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186063894 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2ffbc4bb-e179-543f-bcb5-3aaf6540a8a1" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Slope of a Tangent Line of a Curve at a Given Point"}] :question/id #uuid "9c9b5972-f775-5cbe-8e66-2a0309f24f0e" :question/is-example true :question/math-academy-id "e-142" :question/problem "Find the slope of the tangent to the curve $y = x^2 + \\dfrac {1}{x}$ at the point where $x=2$." :question/worked-solution "Let\n\n$$\nf(x)=x^2+\\dfrac 1 x\n$$\n\nThe slope of the tangent at $x=2$ is equal to $f'(2)$. Computing the derivative, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf^{′}(x) &= \\frac{d}{dx}(x^{2} + \\frac{1}{x}) \\\\\n&= \\frac{d}{dx}(x^{2} + x^{-1}) \\\\\n&= 2 \\cdot x - x^{-2} \\\\\n&= 2x - x^{-2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we evaluate at $x=2$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf^{′}(2) &= 2(2) - (2)^{-2} \\\\\n&= 4 - \\frac{1}{4} \\\\\n&= \\frac{15}{4}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the tangent to the curve is\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{15}{4}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186063897 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3ca13570-d504-53e6-8e02-0f1e85047a3e" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Slope of a Tangent Line of a Curve With Fractional Powers at a Given Point"}] :question/id #uuid "3138f267-3903-510c-86e8-5597d3689262" :question/is-example true :question/math-academy-id "e-143" :question/problem "What is the slope of the tangent to the curve $y = x^4 + 3\\sqrt [3]{x^2}$ at the point $(1,4)$?" :question/worked-solution "This time, we'll use\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d y}{\\textrm d x}\n$$\n\nnotation. First, we compute the derivative, which gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{dy}{dx} &= \\frac{d}{dx}(x^{4} + 3\\sqrt[3]{x^{2}}) \\\\\n&= \\frac{d}{dx}(x^{4} + 3x^{2/3}) \\\\\n&= 4 \\cdot x^{3} + 3 \\cdot \\frac{2}{3} \\cdot x^{-1/3} \\\\\n&= 4x^{3} + 2x^{-1/3}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating at $x=1$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\left.\\frac{dy}{dx}\\right|_{x = 1} &= 4(1)^{3} + 2(1)^{-1/3} \\\\\n&= 4 + 2 \\\\\n&= 6\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the tangent to the curve is $6$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064017 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "00a74f63-a4eb-5894-b4a4-eb4fd297a3f3" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Point on a Curve With a Certain Slope"}] :question/id #uuid "fe999c48-1afd-5949-b4f9-533c09511d95" :question/is-example true :question/math-academy-id "e-5295" :question/problem "Find the $x$-coordinate of the point on the curve $y=3x^2+1$ where the tangent line has a slope of $-1$." :question/worked-solution "Let\n\n$$\nf(x)=3x^2+1\n$$\n\nThe slope of the tangent at the point $x$ is equal to $f'(x)$. Computing the derivative, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf^{′}(x) &= \\frac{d}{dx}(3x^{2} + 1) \\\\\n&= 3\\frac{d}{dx}(x^{2}) + \\frac{d}{dx}(1) \\\\\n&= 3 \\cdot 2x + 0 \\\\\n&= 6x + 0 \\\\\n&= 6x\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now set $f'(x) = -1$ and solve for $x$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf^{′}(x) &= -1 \\\\\n6x &= -1 \\\\\nx &= -\\frac{1}{6}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the tangent is equal to $-1$ at the point where\n\n$$\nx=-\\dfrac 1 6\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186243462 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3ca13570-d504-53e6-8e02-0f1e85047a3e" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Slope of a Tangent Line of a Curve With Fractional Powers at a Given Point"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a5b83ef9-a31d-56c4-87c7-77241ecce359" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243464} {:answer/id #uuid "329e7d38-19ca-553a-86f2-141207cee248" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{11}{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243465} {:answer/id #uuid "b1d58eef-5dd2-5afd-b3ca-6502cebd87fd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243466} {:answer/id #uuid "d87cd597-d123-56ed-8533-214e421cf5b7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243467} {:answer/id #uuid "9f57006c-6315-5da1-94d0-ad6ccfae0cbf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243468}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "329e7d38-19ca-553a-86f2-141207cee248" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{11}{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243465} :answer-field/id #uuid "e5e69722-9a1d-5f47-aa89-e67b3ba96bdc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243463}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ca1a4cf7-f695-5f9c-96b7-ce40ee3a3266" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-102224" :question/problem "What is the slope of the tangent to the curve $y=x-\\sqrt[3]{x}$ at the point $(8,6)?$" :question/worked-solution "This time, we'll use $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ notation. First, we compute the derivative, which gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(x-{x}^{1/3}) \\\\  & =1-\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot {x}^{-2/3} \\\\  & =1-\\frac{1}{3\\sqrt[3]{{x}^{2}}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating at $x=8$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=8} & =1-\\frac{1}{3\\sqrt[3]{{8}^{2}}} \\\\  & =1-\\frac{1}{12} \\\\  & =\\frac{11}{12}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the tangent to the curve is $\\frac{11}{12}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186243469 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "00a74f63-a4eb-5894-b4a4-eb4fd297a3f3" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Point on a Curve With a Certain Slope"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "199d38d3-e5b4-5ea3-a948-5c70b563181c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243471} {:answer/id #uuid "4e6ffa7e-0fce-55cd-a640-3a03cc6acf82" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243472} {:answer/id #uuid "f2f8d4b2-fb5a-5460-86c7-67b173a89b8c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243473} {:answer/id #uuid "881044b0-824d-5590-b864-c2bd0cfc435e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243474} {:answer/id #uuid "66689c14-7ad8-5dd7-a7ff-93a35e417431" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243475}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4e6ffa7e-0fce-55cd-a640-3a03cc6acf82" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243472} :answer-field/id #uuid "daa8cdc8-aaf6-5dfe-b5f8-e11b9c15b24c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243470}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "55adc6dd-898d-5501-8f26-357be5fee8d8" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-102236" :question/problem "Find the $x$-coordinate of the point on the curve $y={x}^{2}-3x+10$ whose tangent has a slope of $-1.$" :question/worked-solution "Let $f(x)={x}^{2}-3x+10.$ The slope of the tangent at the point $x$ is equal to ${f}^{′}(x).$ Computing the derivative, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{2}-3x+10) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{2})-3\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(x)+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(10) \\\\  & =2x-3\\cdot 1+0 \\\\  & =2x-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now set ${f}^{′}(x)=-1$ and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x-3 & =-1 \\\\ 2x & =-1+3 \\\\ 2x & =2 \\\\ x & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the tangent is equal to $-1$ at the point where $x=1.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186243476 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2ffbc4bb-e179-543f-bcb5-3aaf6540a8a1" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Slope of a Tangent Line of a Curve at a Given Point"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c364b142-1525-5b0c-902f-28a1f40d0bf3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243478} {:answer/id #uuid "dbf1a082-f543-5785-8d57-92d3cfb444fa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243479} {:answer/id #uuid "5ee0237d-13df-58ed-a3f3-6153f7c90e00" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243480} {:answer/id #uuid "ce2acb20-bff3-5d3c-af39-44c826c5d598" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243481} {:answer/id #uuid "463aaec1-5db3-5de0-a8b1-51efda9c614a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243482}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dbf1a082-f543-5785-8d57-92d3cfb444fa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243479} :answer-field/id #uuid "fd63b666-f673-52fa-b4fb-b61945be1786" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243477}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a4ac357e-d22e-509f-ad84-7cba73c0f1f9" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-10742" :question/problem "Find the slope of the tangent to the curve $y={x}^{7}-6{x}^{5}-2670x$ at the point where $x=3.$" :question/worked-solution "Let $f(x)={x}^{7}-6{x}^{5}-2670x.$ The slope of the tangent at $x=3$ is equal to ${f}^{′}(3).$ Computing the derivative, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{7}-6{x}^{5}-2670x) \\\\  & =7{x}^{6}-30{x}^{4}-2670.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we evaluate at $x=3$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(3) & =7(3{)}^{6}-30(3{)}^{4}-2670 \\\\  & =5103-2430-2670 \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the tangent to the curve is $3.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186243483 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2ffbc4bb-e179-543f-bcb5-3aaf6540a8a1" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Slope of a Tangent Line of a Curve at a Given Point"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0e5be78f-8dfd-5de7-b5f7-8be44c275cd0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{95}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243485} {:answer/id #uuid "e41a64db-612b-5a0e-93dc-cd2ba7bb302d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{95}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243486} {:answer/id #uuid "31a6f2b0-f613-5ffe-8264-0e32fd132e19" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{93}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243487} {:answer/id #uuid "5da22d19-a503-5c3f-a01b-c5b838d3c356" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{95}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243488} {:answer/id #uuid "540f11ea-c36a-5a0b-bace-4711cb36480a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{97}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243489}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0e5be78f-8dfd-5de7-b5f7-8be44c275cd0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{95}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243485} :answer-field/id #uuid "99768217-d593-5fca-9b10-c4146ae4d86c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243484}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "3729bae5-8a95-5a82-8405-f41738c585fa" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-1853" :question/problem "Find the slope of the tangent to the curve $y=3{x}^{4}-6{x}^{3}+\\frac{1}{x}$ at the point where $x=2.$" :question/worked-solution "Let $f(x)=3{x}^{4}-6{x}^{3}+\\frac{1}{x}.$ The slope of the tangent at $x=2$ is equal to ${f}^{′}(2).$ Computing the derivative, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(3{x}^{4}-6{x}^{3}+\\frac{1}{x}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(3{x}^{4}-6{x}^{3}+{x}^{-1}) \\\\  & =4\\cdot 3{x}^{3}-3\\cdot 6{x}^{2}-{x}^{-2} \\\\  & =12{x}^{3}-18{x}^{2}-{x}^{-2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we evaluate at $x=2$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(2) & =12(2{)}^{3}-18(2{)}^{2}-(2{)}^{-2} \\\\  & =96-72-\\frac{1}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{95}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the tangent to the curve is $\\frac{95}{4}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186243490 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3ca13570-d504-53e6-8e02-0f1e85047a3e" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Slope of a Tangent Line of a Curve With Fractional Powers at a Given Point"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7418489d-97ad-5339-9a74-966cc9d2372a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{20}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243492} {:answer/id #uuid "13abc875-666d-5b54-931f-f95cc75e7e84" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{95}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243493} {:answer/id #uuid "40787c32-64b6-56e0-b577-dcde9b871bb8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{64}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243494} {:answer/id #uuid "48ca82a7-bb3b-5766-909c-60945c33fdb4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{19}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243495} {:answer/id #uuid "9f9c58a0-71fb-547a-9a62-4558b84dba32" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{62}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243496}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9f9c58a0-71fb-547a-9a62-4558b84dba32" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{62}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243496} :answer-field/id #uuid "c62a35e7-6f9d-5b23-8112-746840662d13" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243491}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c57c9928-5e43-54b8-b676-a2f59a2207b1" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-1901" :question/problem "What is the slope of the tangent to the curve $y=5{x}^{4}+\\sqrt[3]{{x}^{2}}$ at the point $(1,6)?$" :question/worked-solution "This time, we'll use $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ notation. First, we compute the derivative, which gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(5{x}^{4}+\\sqrt[3]{{x}^{2}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(5{x}^{4}+{x}^{2/3}) \\\\  & =4\\cdot 5{x}^{3}+\\frac{2}{3}\\cdot {x}^{-1/3} \\\\  & =20{x}^{3}+\\frac{2{x}^{-1/3}}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating at $x=1$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=1} & =20(1{)}^{3}+\\frac{2(1{)}^{-1/3}}{3} \\\\  & =20+\\frac{2}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{62}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the tangent to the curve is $\\frac{62}{3}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186243497 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3ca13570-d504-53e6-8e02-0f1e85047a3e" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Slope of a Tangent Line of a Curve With Fractional Powers at a Given Point"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a7d1d1cb-00e1-5940-8f1f-750eece037ad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243499}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a7d1d1cb-00e1-5940-8f1f-750eece037ad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243499} :answer-field/id #uuid "cb96b9ad-46dd-5b58-9c08-3da5a25e227d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243498}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a306f416-baa0-512a-a10c-37750b4fcbfa" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-304130" :question/problem "Find the exact value of the slope $m$ of the tangent to the curve $y=4x-2\\sqrt{x}$ at the point $(4,12).$\n\n$m=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "This time, we'll use $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ notation. First, we compute the derivative, which gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(4x-2\\sqrt{x}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(4x-2{x}^{1/2}) \\\\  & =4-2\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}{x}^{-1/2} \\\\  & =4-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating at $x=4$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=4} & =4-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{4}} \\\\  & =4-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope $m$ of the tangent to the curve at the point $(4,12)$ is\n\n$$\nm={\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=4}=\\frac{7}{2}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186243500 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2ffbc4bb-e179-543f-bcb5-3aaf6540a8a1" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Slope of a Tangent Line of a Curve at a Given Point"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "de3930b4-cefd-57a2-bb86-0a55d7cebeee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243502} {:answer/id #uuid "3cd04b74-99e7-542c-adbe-00b180dd95d4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243503}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3cd04b74-99e7-542c-adbe-00b180dd95d4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243503} :answer-field/id #uuid "ed81aec2-98ac-5f99-8f51-90d964f589a3" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243501}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e799e759-0266-55ca-b4f9-da847ab184cf" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-342107" :question/problem "Find the exact value of the slope $m$ of the tangent to the curve $y={x}^{6}-4{x}^{4}+8{x}^{2}-4$ at the point where $x=-1.$\n\n$m=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Let $f(x)=({x}^{2}-1{)}^{3}+3.$ The slope of the tangent at $x=-1$ is equal to ${f}^{′}(-1).$ Computing the derivative, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{d}{dx}\\,({x}^{6}-4{x}^{4}+8{x}^{2}-4) \\\\  & =6{x}^{5}-4(4{x}^{3})+8(2x)-0 \\\\  & =6{x}^{5}-16{x}^{3}+16x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we evaluate at $x=-1$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(-1) & =6(-1{)}^{5}-16(-1{)}^{3}+16(-1) \\\\  & =-6+16-16 \\\\  & =-6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope $m$ of the tangent to the curve at $x=-1$ is\n\n$$\nm={f}^{′}(-1)=-6.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186243504 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2ffbc4bb-e179-543f-bcb5-3aaf6540a8a1" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Slope of a Tangent Line of a Curve at a Given Point"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c209f512-d7c5-52a5-93fc-93cd21008a62" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243506}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c209f512-d7c5-52a5-93fc-93cd21008a62" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243506} :answer-field/id #uuid "192143f5-1603-5c59-97a2-a7e83acd5a68" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243505}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "cd6ecfb6-9213-52aa-9fe9-2ff9956ebe7e" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-342937" :question/problem "Find the exact value of the slope $m$ of the tangent to the curve $y=-2{x}^{2}+\\frac{1}{(x-2{)}^{2}}$ at the point where $x=3.$\n\n$m=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Let $f(x)=-2{x}^{2}+\\frac{1}{(x-2{)}^{2}}.$ The slope of the tangent at $x=3$ is equal to ${f}^{′}(3).$ Computing the derivative, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-2{x}^{2}+\\frac{1}{(x-2{)}^{2}}) \\\\  & =-4x+(-2(x-2{)}^{-3}) \\\\  & =-4x-\\frac{2}{(x-2{)}^{3}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we evaluate at $x=3$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(3) & =-4(3)-\\frac{2}{(3-2{)}^{3}} \\\\  & =-12-2 \\\\  & =-14.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope $m$ of the tangent to the curve at $x=3$ is\n\n$$\nm={f}^{′}(3)=-14.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186243507 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2ffbc4bb-e179-543f-bcb5-3aaf6540a8a1" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Slope of a Tangent Line of a Curve at a Given Point"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8f788e86-75a6-58cd-9e89-4b26cbc66552" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{82}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243509} {:answer/id #uuid "caf609cb-391d-50c1-a836-806b764ebeb6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{80}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243510}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "caf609cb-391d-50c1-a836-806b764ebeb6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{80}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243510} :answer-field/id #uuid "7c478e5d-8b04-503c-89a6-560a259dd56a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243508}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "08c9ff7a-25a1-590d-aa94-e0a9cfe8132e" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-342942" :question/problem "Find the exact value of the slope $m$ of the tangent to the curve $y=2{x}^{4}-7{x}^{3}-6{x}^{2}-\\frac{1}{x}$ at the point where $x=3.$\n\n$m=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Let $f(x)=2{x}^{4}-7{x}^{3}-6{x}^{2}-\\frac{1}{x}.$ The slope of the tangent at $x=3$ is equal to ${f}^{′}(3).$ Computing the derivative, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2{x}^{4}-7{x}^{3}-6{x}^{2}-\\frac{1}{x}) \\\\  & =2\\cdot 4{x}^{3}-7\\cdot 3{x}^{2}-6\\cdot 2x+{x}^{-2} \\\\  & =8{x}^{3}-21{x}^{2}-12x+\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we evaluate at $x=3$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(3) & =8({3}^{3})-21({3}^{2})-12(3)+\\frac{1}{{3}^{2}} \\\\  & =216-189-36+\\frac{1}{9} \\\\  & =-9+\\frac{1}{9} \\\\  & =-\\frac{80}{9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope $m$ of the tangent to the curve at $x=3$ is\n\n$$\nm={f}^{′}(3)=-\\frac{80}{9}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186243511 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3ca13570-d504-53e6-8e02-0f1e85047a3e" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Slope of a Tangent Line of a Curve With Fractional Powers at a Given Point"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c811dac0-c30a-530a-8265-7ae505b3bba2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{25}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243513}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c811dac0-c30a-530a-8265-7ae505b3bba2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{25}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243513} :answer-field/id #uuid "c8f0e32a-50db-5cb5-81ae-aba008cc5a8c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243512}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "eff718aa-3718-5a5e-a18a-88e8832c13a4" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-343079" :question/problem "Find the exact value of the slope $m$ of the tangent to the curve $y=5\\sqrt{x}-10{x}^{3/4}$ at the point $(16,-60).$\n\n$m=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "This time, we'll use $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ notation. First, we compute the derivative, which gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(5\\sqrt{x}-10{x}^{3/4}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(5{x}^{1/2}-10{x}^{3/4}) \\\\  & =5\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}{x}^{-1/2}-10\\cdot \\frac{3}{4}{x}^{-1/4} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}{x}^{-1/2}-\\frac{15}{2}{x}^{-1/4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating at $x=16$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=16} & =\\frac{5}{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}-\\frac{15}{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{25}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope $m$ of the tangent to the curve at the point $(16,-60)$ is\n\n$$\nm={\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=16}=-\\frac{25}{8}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186243514 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "00a74f63-a4eb-5894-b4a4-eb4fd297a3f3" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Point on a Curve With a Certain Slope"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "07a2a4a8-e2d2-56cf-9ebb-8c2056aa5911" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243516}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "07a2a4a8-e2d2-56cf-9ebb-8c2056aa5911" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243516} :answer-field/id #uuid "3e30b918-faca-505c-be4a-276ec08dcf8d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243515}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0b6a548d-8404-5ccf-b01f-49296c1fec20" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-343735" :question/problem "Find the exact value of the $x$-coordinate of the point on the curve $y=2{x}^{2}+4x-3$ whose tangent has a slope of $1.$\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Let $f(x)=2{x}^{2}+4x-3.$ The slope of the tangent at the point $x$ is equal to ${f}^{′}(x).$ Computing the derivative, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2{x}^{2}+4x-3) \\\\  & =2\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{2})+4\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(x) \\\\  & =2(2x)+4(1) \\\\  & =4x+4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now set ${f}^{′}(x)=1$ and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4x+4 & =1 \\\\ 4x & =-3 \\\\ x & =-\\frac{3}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the tangent is equal to $1$ at the point where $x=-\\frac{3}{4}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186243517 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "00a74f63-a4eb-5894-b4a4-eb4fd297a3f3" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Point on a Curve With a Certain Slope"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "46f323bc-bde6-5a1f-bcca-a5297b99d0d2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243519}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "46f323bc-bde6-5a1f-bcca-a5297b99d0d2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243519} :answer-field/id #uuid "11a57ec6-a9fc-5a80-b71c-39f47076dcc2" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243518}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "33387ec2-9f2b-5805-9498-c0c70b4916a5" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-343737" :question/problem "Find the **positive** $x$-coordinate of the point on the curve $y={x}^{3}+{x}^{2}+14x-6$ whose tangent has a slope of $22.$\n\n$\\,x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Let $f(x)={x}^{3}+{x}^{2}+14x-6.$ The slope of the tangent at the point $x$ is equal to ${f}^{′}(x).$ Computing the derivative, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{3}+{x}^{2}+14x-6) \\\\  & =3{x}^{2}+2x+14.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now set ${f}^{′}(x)=22$ and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{x}^{2}+2x+14 & =22 \\\\ 3{x}^{2}+2x-8 & =0 \\\\ (3x-4)(x+2) & =0 \\\\ x & =-2,\\,\\frac{4}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the positive $x$-coordinate of the points whose tangent has a slope of $6,$ is\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{4}{3}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186243520 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "00a74f63-a4eb-5894-b4a4-eb4fd297a3f3" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Point on a Curve With a Certain Slope"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fb85a957-3069-518f-817d-bcf6a6a1fdc7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243522} {:answer/id #uuid "646ed71b-942c-5b68-b1c8-1d35306ba910" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243523} {:answer/id #uuid "2fd17713-9b91-50a5-9814-fceceb72ad43" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243524} {:answer/id #uuid "322d71c2-3ba4-54b7-85e9-24089567f9fc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-3,\\,1." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243525} {:answer/id #uuid "8badc995-bc76-5a62-8e38-6d4b6bf18bbf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-1,\\,3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243526}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8badc995-bc76-5a62-8e38-6d4b6bf18bbf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-1,\\,3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243526} :answer-field/id #uuid "b13f85ef-6c81-56b7-b9c8-8f5ad700e1d3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243521}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "43110fcc-7c49-5c09-8f25-68d9ac38bcdf" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-48817" :question/problem "Find the $x$-coordinates of the points on the curve $y=-2{x}^{3}+6{x}^{2}+20x-1$ whose tangent has a slope of $2.$" :question/worked-solution "Let $f(x)=-2{x}^{3}+6{x}^{2}+20x-1.$ The slope of the tangent at the point $x$ is equal to ${f}^{′}(x).$ Computing the derivative, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-2{x}^{3}+6{x}^{2}+20x-1) \\\\  & =-2\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{3})+6\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{2})+20\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(x)-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(1) \\\\  & =-2\\cdot 3{x}^{2}+6\\cdot 2x+20\\cdot 1-0 \\\\  & =-6{x}^{2}+12x+20.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now set ${f}^{′}(x)=2$ and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-6{x}^{2}+12x+20 & =2 \\\\ -6{x}^{2}+12x+18 & =0 \\\\ -6({x}^{2}-2x-3) & =0 \\\\ -6(x+1)(x-3) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the tangent is equal to $2$ at the points where $x=-1,3.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186243527 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "00a74f63-a4eb-5894-b4a4-eb4fd297a3f3" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Point on a Curve With a Certain Slope"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "52d1872c-d026-516d-a130-bd4855e31bef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243529} {:answer/id #uuid "132312c6-8032-506e-b1ef-4d1d167e4c07" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243530} {:answer/id #uuid "51693466-116b-57f2-af25-41811f369732" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243531} {:answer/id #uuid "e33b97fd-f936-50fa-8eac-70c65ef903ff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243532} {:answer/id #uuid "5866e2ae-1a57-518c-ae97-b188da492bf1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243533}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "52d1872c-d026-516d-a130-bd4855e31bef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243529} :answer-field/id #uuid "526fb417-5991-53f0-bbc2-ed4b4e29bbdd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243528}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "6595768f-0869-5bfa-b0ba-7eabfdbb153e" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-48970" :question/problem "Find the positive $x$-coordinate of the point on the curve $y=8{x}^{3}-3{x}^{2}-12x-4$ whose tangent has a slope of $6.$" :question/worked-solution "Let $f(x)=8{x}^{3}-3{x}^{2}-12x-4.$ The slope of the tangent at the point $x$ is equal to ${f}^{′}(x).$ Computing the derivative, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(8{x}^{3}-3{x}^{2}-12x-4) \\\\  & =8\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{3})-3\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{2})-12\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(x)-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(4) \\\\  & =8\\cdot 3{x}^{2}-3\\cdot 2x-12\\cdot 1-0 \\\\  & =24{x}^{2}-6x-12.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now set ${f}^{′}(x)=6$ and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}24{x}^{2}-6x-12 & =6 \\\\ 24{x}^{2}-6x-18 & =0 \\\\ 6(4{x}^{2}-x-3) & =0 \\\\ 6(x-1)(4x+3) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the tangent is equal to $6$ at the point where $x=1$ and $x=-\\frac{3}{4}.$ Since $x>0$, our answer is $x=1.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186243534 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3ca13570-d504-53e6-8e02-0f1e85047a3e" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Slope of a Tangent Line of a Curve With Fractional Powers at a Given Point"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1bd9fc4e-a40c-5a06-87a3-071208d672aa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243536} {:answer/id #uuid "750fb34e-0042-5aed-b5c0-c69997c2bb46" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243537} {:answer/id #uuid "afb099ab-4060-53a0-a4a8-28c96e400167" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{13}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243538} {:answer/id #uuid "c9e39637-7911-56a6-88fb-d56a55591468" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{13}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243539} {:answer/id #uuid "98ab361f-9602-5ec5-ba66-b865d93ad4a2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{7}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243540}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c9e39637-7911-56a6-88fb-d56a55591468" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{13}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243539} :answer-field/id #uuid "00cd5da6-f3e0-57d0-a7a3-6ba8f5a8a3e9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243535}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3f11bb35-802f-5628-97dc-b167fe087d7d" :question/is-example false :question/math-academy-id "q-70535" :question/problem "What is the slope of the tangent to the curve $y={x}^{2}-3x+6\\sqrt{x}$ at the point $(4,16)?$" :question/worked-solution "This time, we'll use $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ notation. First, we compute the derivative, which gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{2}-3x+6\\sqrt{x}) \\\\  & =2\\cdot x-3+\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 6{x}^{-1/2} \\\\  & =2x-3+3{x}^{-1/2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating at $x=4$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=4} & =2(4)-3+3(4{)}^{-1/2} \\\\  & =8-3+\\frac{3}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{13}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the tangent to the curve is $\\frac{13}{2}.$"}]}
